      solid-angle average             = nu_ex*(L_nu + 3)/3
      trace/3                         = nu_ex*(L_nu + 3)/3
  [OK] W4d *** AND THE REASON THAT MATTERS: THE QUMOND MONOPOLE IS IDENTICALLY THE MI ORIENTATION AVERAGE. *** Proved symbolically, by carrying out the solid-angle integral of the MI response tensor's radial boost and finding it equals trace/3 = nu_ex(1 + L_nu/3) -- exactly the combination W4b just measured as QUMOND's delta-function source strength. Both objects ARE the trace of the same response tensor, so in the deep-EFE limit the orientation-averaged two-body force of modified inertia and of QUMOND is THE SAME NUMBER, 1.341427. No sample size can separate them on that statistic

