  symbolic, for ANY monotone kernel (L = L_mu > 0):  MI = 1/(L + 1),  QUMOND = 2*(L + 1)/(L + 2),  AQUAL = sqrt(1+L)
      1 - MI      = L/(L + 1)          > 0
      QUMOND - 1  = L/(L + 2)          > 0
      AQUAL^2 - QUMOND^2 = L**2*(L + 1)/(L + 2)**2   > 0
  [OK] W5 *** THE SIGN OPPOSITION IS A THEOREM, NOT A ROUTE A ACCIDENT. *** Symbolically, for any monotone kernel: 1 - MI = L/(1+L) > 0, QUMOND - 1 = L/(2+L) > 0 and AQUAL^2 - QUMOND^2 = L^2(1+L)/(2+L)^2 > 0, so MI < 1 < QUMOND < AQUAL strictly whenever L_mu > 0. Corroborated on all 16 numeric cells (4 kernels x 2 a0 footings x 2 frozen g_ext conventions). A measured SIGN therefore discriminates with no kernel commitment, no a0 footing choice and no mass model at all
